  "jsspace.configuration.failures": "Rocket failures",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.burning_up": "Burning up on re-entry",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.burning_up.tooltip": "A capsule that comes down through air with no heat shield, or with the wrong one for that air, burns up.\nOff, such a capsule cannot begin to come down, and stays where it is.",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.crash_landings": "Crash landings",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.crash_landings.tooltip": "A lander with no legs, or with no propellant left to slow down, crashes.\nOff, such a lander cannot begin its landing, and stays where it is.",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.damaged_tanks_explode": "Damaged tanks explode",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.damaged_tanks_explode.tooltip": "A damaged oxygen tank used anyway explodes, destroying the rocket and harming what is around it.\nOff, a rocket with a damaged tank does not leave the ground.",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.too_heavy_to_lift": "Too heavy to lift",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.too_heavy_to_lift.tooltip": "A rocket whose thrust is less than its weight lights its engines and stays on the pad, burning its propellant.\nOff, its engines do not light, and nothing is spent.",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.tooltip": "What a badly built or badly kept rocket does: always a consequence of a choice, never bad luck.",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.worn_stages_fail": "Worn stages fail",
  "jsspace.configuration.failures.worn_stages_fail.tooltip": "Every flight wears the parts of a reused stage: inspected and repaired, it keeps flying; past its limit unrepaired, an engine shuts down or a tank cracks.\nOff, reused stages never wear.",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar": "Rocket Hangar",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.lowest": "Lowest bay",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.lowest.tooltip": "The lowest a Rocket Hangar's bay may be, from its floor to its roof, in blocks.",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.narrowest": "Narrowest bay",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.narrowest.tooltip": "The narrowest a Rocket Hangar's bay may be, across and deep, inside its walls, in blocks.",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.tallest": "Tallest bay",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.tallest.tooltip": "The tallest a Rocket Hangar's bay may be, from its floor to its roof, in blocks.",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.tooltip": "How small and how large a Rocket Hangar's bay may be.",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.widest": "Widest bay",
  "jsspace.configuration.hangar.widest.tooltip": "The widest a Rocket Hangar's bay may be, across and deep, inside its walls, in blocks.\nA wider one measures more of its walls each time it looks at itself.",
  "jsspace.configuration.launch": "Launch",
  "jsspace.configuration.launch.launch_damage": "Launch damage",
  "jsspace.configuration.launch.launch_damage.tooltip": "A pad with no flame trench and no deluge is damaged at launch, and so is what stands around it.\nOff, the pad takes no harm, whatever it is built with.",
  "jsspace.configuration.launch.no_launch_in_thunderstorms": "No launch in a thunderstorm",
  "jsspace.configuration.launch.no_launch_in_thunderstorms.tooltip": "The launch panel holds the countdown while a thunderstorm is over the pad.\nOff, a rocket launches in any weather.",
  "jsspace.configuration.launch.tooltip": "What a launch does to its pad, and the weather it waits for.",
  "jsspace.configuration.life_support": "Life support",
  "jsspace.configuration.life_support.flames_need_air": "Flames need air",
  "jsspace.configuration.life_support.flames_need_air.tooltip": "Torches, lanterns, candles and campfires go out where the air holds too little oxygen to burn: in a vacuum, in the thin air of Mars, in a room whose air runs short.\nOff, they burn anywhere, as on the Earth.",
  "jsspace.configuration.life_support.tooltip": "What the air of other worlds does to what burns in it.",
  "jsspace.configuration.orbit": "Orbit",
  "jsspace.configuration.orbit.debris": "Debris",
  "jsspace.configuration.orbit.debris.tooltip": "A destroyed satellite leaves debris in orbit, which strikes what passes through it and multiplies.\nOff, a destroyed satellite leaves nothing behind.",
  "jsspace.configuration.orbit.laser_satellite_weapon": "Laser Satellite as a weapon",
  "jsspace.configuration.orbit.laser_satellite_weapon.tooltip": "The Laser Satellite may strike players and what they built.\nOff, for a server without PvP, it harms no player and nothing a player built.",
  "jsspace.configuration.orbit.tooltip": "What is left in orbit, and what a satellite may strike.",
  "jsspace.configuration.rockets": "Rockets",
  "jsspace.configuration.rockets.falling_stages_do_damage": "Falling stages do damage",
  "jsspace.configuration.rockets.falling_stages_do_damage.tooltip": "A stage that falls with no fall zone and no platform to land on leaves a crater where it comes down.\nOff, it only lies where it fell, as wreckage.",
  "jsspace.configuration.rockets.tooltip": "What a rocket's spent stages do where they fall.",
  "jsspace.configuration.series": "The series",
  "jsspace.configuration.series.industrial_chain_only": "Industrial chain only",
  "jsspace.configuration.series.industrial_chain_only.tooltip": "Whether, with J's Industrial installed, its chains become the only path for what both mods make.\nOff, what J's Space makes it makes its own way too.",
  "jsspace.configuration.series.tooltip": "How J's Space shares its work with the other mods of the series.",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel": "Travel",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel.cruise_events": "Cruise events",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel.cruise_events.tooltip": "Solar storms, micrometeoroids and failures come on the way between worlds.\nOff, the cruise is quiet.",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel.fast_travel": "Fast travel",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel.fast_travel.tooltip": "Whether a rocket or a starship skips its cruise and arrives at once.\nOff, the cruise is flown, with its time and its events.",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel.landing_needs_the_essentials": "Landing needs the essentials",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel.landing_needs_the_essentials.tooltip": "A crew cannot land on a world until its team knows the world's atmosphere, temperature, radiation, gravity and relief.\nOff, a crew may land on any world it reaches, known or not.",
  "jsspace.configuration.travel.tooltip": "The way between worlds, and what a crew must know before it lands.",
  "jsspace.configuration.worlds": "Worlds",
  "jsspace.configuration.worlds.dust_on_mars": "Dust on Mars",
  "jsspace.configuration.worlds.dust_on_mars.tooltip": "Dust settles on solar panels on Mars, and now and then a dust storm covers the whole planet.\nOff, Mars has no dust on its panels and no dust storms.",
  "jsspace.configuration.worlds.naming_hidden_worlds": "Naming hidden worlds",
  "jsspace.configuration.worlds.naming_hidden_worlds.tooltip": "The first team to find a hidden world names it.\nOff, every world keeps its default name.",
  "jsspace.configuration.worlds.tooltip": "What the worlds do, and who names the hidden ones.",
